  "verses": [
    {
      "number": 1,
      "pali": "Linked Discourses 7.14",
      "english": "Linked Discourses 7.14"
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "pali": "Mahāsāla Sutta",
      "english": "Very Rich"
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Near Sāvatthī. Then a certain very rich brahman—shabby, shabbily dressed—went to the Blessed One and, on arrival, exchanged courteous greetings with him. After this exchange of friendly greetings & courtesies, he sat to one side. As he was sitting there the Blessed One said to him, “Why, brahman, are you shabby & shabbily dressed?”"
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“Just now, Master Gotama, my four sons—at their wives instigation—threw me out of the house.”"
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“In that case, brahman, memorize these verses and then recite them when a large assembly of people have gathered in the town hall and your sons are sitting there, too."
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“Those whose birth"
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "I delighted in"
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "—whose growth I desired—"
    },
    {
      "number": 9,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "at their wives instigation"
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "have chased me away,"
    },
    {
      "number": 11,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "as dogs would swine."
    },
    {
      "number": 12,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Wicked & vile,"
    },
    {
      "number": 13,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "though they call me ‘Dad’:"
    },
    {
      "number": 14,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "demons in the disguise of sons"
    },
    {
      "number": 15,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "who abandon me in old age."
    },
    {
      "number": 16,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "As an old horse"
    },
    {
      "number": 17,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "of no more use"
    },
    {
      "number": 18,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "is deprived of fodder,"
    },
    {
      "number": 19,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "so the elderly father"
    },
    {
      "number": 20,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "of those foolish boys"
    },
    {
      "number": 21,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "begs at other people’s homes."
    },
    {
      "number": 22,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "My staff serves me better"
    },
    {
      "number": 23,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "than those disobedient sons."
    },
    {
      "number": 24,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "It fends off"
    },
    {
      "number": 25,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "ferocious bulls"
    },
    {
      "number": 26,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "& ferocious curs."
    },
    {
      "number": 27,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "In the dark it goes before me;"
    },
    {
      "number": 28,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "down steep slopes, it gives support."
    },
    {
      "number": 29,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Through the power of my staff,"
    },
    {
      "number": 30,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "when I stumble"
    },
    {
      "number": 31,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "I still stand firm.”"
    },
    {
      "number": 32,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Then the very rich brahman, having memorized these verses in the presence of the Blessed One, recited them when a large assembly of people had gathered in the town hall and his sons were sitting there, too:"
    },
    {
